/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-49-* ''After a machine restart'' the session scratchpad empties and every worktree under it vanishes. Durable state lives in git and in the session folder; a resumed lane re-reads its resume sheet, provisions a fresh worktree at HEAD, and rebuilds.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-50-* ''O-takiage'' closes every lane and every settle as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-otakiage` names it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-51-* ''Fetch before you act, and again before you push.'' Another lane can merge into the work branch between two turns; a lane that pushes past it, or reasons from a stale origin, cures the wrong tree.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-52-* ''A local green proves the tree it read.'' A worktree whose `node_modules` link into another checkout tests that checkout's build; every vitest config refuses a stale or foreign `dist` (`tools/vitest-dist-guard.mjs`). Provision lane worktrees with `tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-53-* ''One red in CI masks every package after it.'' `pnpm test` runs the packages in order and stops at the first red, so a cured red can reveal the next. Before pushing a cure, run the packages that come after it, or read the next CI run whole.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-54-* ''Read the containers' own logs before naming a cause.'' A held-out cell uploads each container's log as an artifact (`gh run download <run> -n <cell>`); tallying each container's own lines split the carriage red where the witness's verdict could not. An in-process reproduction holds one Repo, so it cannot show a defect that lives between a CLI process and a running daemon.
