/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem:99:A cloud session opens on branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, stands the house from the boot seed, reads the roadmap's #/the-attractor, #/cold-start and #/rulings, this carrier whole (#/the-lane-law binds it), `working-procedures`, and its lane's kit, then walks its lane below. It leads as the Episkopos over the cloud crew `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-100-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-101-A cloud lane commits on its OWN branch, `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--<lane>`, cut from `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, and pushes that branch alone; CI and held-out fire on it. It shards each burst with `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>-<n>` and reads `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha> --branch <branch>`. Where the container's `gh` holds no login, each burst pushes the lane branch instead: CI's own E2E job runs the same five shards behind its merge gate, and the lane reads CI and held-out through the GitHub connector. The committed `.claude/settings.json` runs `tools/stash-guard.mjs` before every Bash call; a refusal from it stops that step. It never pushes `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` or `main`: the controller merges each lane branch after reading its three readings. Before its final push it merges `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` into its lane branch. It lists canon and changelog lines for the roadmap and `CHANGELOG.md` in its handback, and edits neither. It stops at a clean boundary when context runs short and hands back in the lane law's shape, with its lane branch and head.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-102-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-103-!!! Lane `wire-socket` ~ past lane
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-104-Train W's assembled cutover landed as PR #44: every vessel socket opens through the sealed face gate on one handshake, fleet join serves every face, a fresh browser device stands at the floor, and a herm answers the knock where a Nexus carries it. The roadmap's `W` rows name what stays owed.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-105-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-106-!!! Lane `carriage-fold` ~ a local session's lane
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-107-Kit: <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/carriage-fold-lane">>. Roadmap row `W18`: the carrier folds walk the roll anchors (PR #50, merged 2026-10-19), and `P20`'s gate half reads a place contract across a roll (PR #54), so held-out reads green on every driver; DreamDom-Wright builds `F6` on lane `holder-owner`, owing the deliberate cross-epoch held-out cell beside it. A lane under `mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`: its own sub-branch, the work swarm's build pair in one worktree, the other lineage's read, the overwatch, a pull request.
