/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-165-A session can close and a fresh one boot from carriers; a ''live'' handoff lets both stand for a while, so the new seat can ask the old one what no carrier caught. The seat passes by explicit word, never by drift.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-166-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-167-# ''One controller at a time.'' Only the seat-holder pushes the feature branch, fills lane slots and commits to `CHANGELOG.md` or the roadmap. The other session reads, asks, and works only lanes the seat-holder hands it by name.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-168-# ''The outgoing seat trues #/state'' in this carrier, commits it, and names its lanes in flight: which will finish under it, and which pass to the incoming seat with their resume sheets.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem:169:# ''The incoming seat reads first'': the boot seed, the roadmap's cold start, and this carrier whole, #/the-lane-law included. Then it asks the outgoing seat, by session name over the message channel, whatever stays unclear: a lane's intent, a house reading's reason, a red that looked like a flake.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-170-# ''The seat passes by message.'' The outgoing seat sends "the seat passes to <session>" once no push stands in flight and every lane it keeps has a named owner; the incoming seat answers "the seat holds". Until that answer, the outgoing seat still holds it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-171-# ''Lanes keep their spirit.'' A running lane answers the session that launched it. A lane that passes gets a new lead launched by the incoming seat from its resume sheet, never a message to a subagent of another session.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem-172-# ''Questions flow both ways after the pass''; the outgoing session may keep a lane to finish, and reports its handback to the new seat-holder as a lane would.
