/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-56-** ''Podge'' carries Yin and Ka, the Eristic face: what moves. It reads what the work does under change (the race, the other caller, the epoch that rolls, the case left out, the control that never bites).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-57-** ''Spin'' carries Ba. Each face reads alone first; then the pair trades: each takes the other's findings, confirms or refutes each against the source, and reads the other's ground for what its own face missed. Orthogonal findings both stand; tensioned ones get measured, never voted; a finding one face alone raised stays a lead.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-58-* ''Overwatch.'' The Opus controller reads every crew's handback and every chunk's diff before it merges, and names each finding it would block on. Work that moves a fact between processes or threads (a writer and its readers, a composer and its islands, a verb and its route) always takes the controller's own read of the crossing, since a module's own reads catch its contract and miss its crossings.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-59-* ''The battery runs at the wave's end, on the shards.'' A wave writes every red and its control as it builds, since a red names the specification, and runs nothing between its fixes. At its end it runs locally only what CI cannot: the build, and each red's proof against its base (the red files alone over the pre-cure tree). It pushes once, and CI carries the battery: the lane CI runs every package suite, the witnesses and the tool self-tests; `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>` spreads both e2e sets across shards; held-out runs its cells. The wave reads every verdict, cures what reads red, pushes again only once no run flies, and hands back when CI and held-out read green.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-60-* ''The fresh read and the train.'' A lane's handback takes a fresh reader's whole-lane read before it merges; a HOLD sends the findings back as the next launch, up to five launches, with the uncertainties talked out between them. The controller then merges ready lanes in trains (#/the-lanes).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-61-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-62-<<~/ahu>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-63-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:64:<<~ ahu #/the-lens-law>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-65-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-66-!! The lens law ~ why several eyes outweigh one
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-67-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-68-# ''Correlated eyes count once.'' Two seats of one lineage share their blind spots; a finding both report still reads as one lead. A second lineage reads with a different prior, so its agreement carries weight and its dissent marks where to look.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-69-# ''One eye alone yields a lead, never ground.'' Ground needs a second eye through another lens, or a measurement.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-70-# ''The reader built nothing.'' A reviewer that built the piece reads its own intent into the diff.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-71-# ''Framing without conclusion.'' A second researcher gets the question and the framing, never the first one's answer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-72-# ''A clean read clears nothing.'' A reader's finding earns a look, and its silence lands nothing. The lead re-derives any list a seat proposes to destroy, and a second eye reads the script.
--
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-119-# ''Canon follows the code in the same burst.'' A census over every carrier names each burned symbol, file, flag and variable; each live line re-trues to what stands, citing file and symbol, never a line number.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-120-# ''Testimony stays.'' A testimony carrier, a dated scout and a dated crossing row keep their words; the house re-trues their frame, never their body.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-121-# ''A witness that catches burned names burns itself'' once it reads green over the tree.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-122-# ''Roadmaps move what stands finished'' onto their own o-takiage shelf, verbatim, and keep only what stays owed on the road.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-123-# ''Scratch returns too.'' A seat's worktree leaves only after a census proves every file it holds landed; plain `git worktree remove`, never `--force`; a worktree that initialized submodules waits for the operator's hand.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-124-
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem-125-<<~/ahu>>
