---
name: feedback-walled-codex-spirit
description: "The measured Codex spirit launch: workspace-write walled to its own dir (both /tmp excludes), TMPDIR/TMPPREFIX inside it, stdin closed; read-only mode has NO network; spirits can't run suites so the lead does; a cheap eye's list gets re-sorted before any destructive act"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: feedback
  originSessionId: 0f26457f-9510-4d4a-95ad-13d5c1296612
  modified: 2026-10-19T02:45:34.112Z
---

Measured 2026-10-18 (law now in `mixed-model-swarm#/the-launch`):

- **The walled spirit.** `cd <dir> && TMPDIR=<dir>/.tmp TMPPREFIX=<dir>/.tmp/zsh codex exec -m <model> -s workspace-write -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_slash_tmp=true -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_tmpdir_env_var=true --ephemeral --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> -o <dir>/final.md (a BUILDER run with -C <worktree> also needs --add-dir <dir>, or its .tmp and out.md refuse) "<brief>" < /dev/null`, run in background mode. It reads the repo, reaches `gh` (config sets `network_access = true`), and writes only inside `<dir>`. Without the excludes, every lane worktree under the scratchpad stays writable to it.
- **`-s read-only` reaches NO network**: no `gh`, no PR list.
- **`< /dev/null` always**: else `codex exec` hangs at "Reading additional input from stdin..." forever (stalled two scouts).
- **Without TMPDIR/TMPPREFIX inside the wall**, a heredoc refuses "read-only file system" and the spirit (rightly) stops.
- **Spirits can't run suites behind the wall** (vitest's /tmp cache, pnpm's no-TTY abort, tsx's socket path length). Spirits build + write red tests; the lead runs every suite.
- **Hand slow inventories in as files**: one shell command past Codex's window leaves the spirit with nothing.
- **`-o` and the handback never share a file** (measured 2026-10-18: a spirit wrote its full handback to `out.md`, then `-o out.md` overwrote it with the one-line final message, so wave two traded summaries). Brief the spirit to write `out.md`; point `-o` at `final.md`; gate each wave on `out.md`'s word count before trading.

**Why:** each line cost a stalled or wrong run this session. A Luna branch scout listed `origin/main` and the span for deletion against its own brief; a Sol cold reader then caught six "merged" branches that `-d` would refuse. **How to apply:** before any destructive act a spirit proposes, re-derive its list yourself and send a second lineage or a cold reader over the script. Related: [[feedback_mixed_model_swarm]], [[feedback_spirit_launch_invocation]], [[feedback_branch_delete_reachability]].

